.TH GSP670 1 "2026-10-11" "0.1.0" "GSP 670 Control Utility"
.SH NAME
gsp670 \- EPOS|Sennheiser GSP 670 headset control utility for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gsp670
[\fIOPTIONS\fP] \fICOMMAND\fP [\fIARGS\fP]...
.PP
.B gsp670
\fBinfo\fP [\fB\-\-json\fP]
.PP
.B gsp670
\fBstatus\fP [\fB\-\-json\fP]
.PP
.B gsp670
\fBbattery\fP [\fB\-\-json\fP]
.PP
.B gsp670
\fBcontrols\fP \fIlist\fP | \fIget\fP \fICONTROL\fP | \fIset\fP \fICONTROL\fP \fIVALUE\fP
.PP
.B gsp670
\fBmonitor\fP
.PP
.B gsp670
\fBevents\fP [\fB\-\-count\fP \fIN\fP]
.PP
.B gsp670
\fBprotocol\fP \fIinspect\fP
.PP
.B gsp670
\fBlog\fP [\fB\-\-level\fP \fILEVEL\fP] [\fB\-\-message\fP]
.PP
.B gsp670
\fBtest\fP \fIaudio\fP
.PP
.B gsp670
{\fB\-\-version\fP | \fB\-\-help\fP}
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gsp670
is a command-line utility for controlling the EPOS|Sennheiser GSP 670 wireless gaming headset from Linux. It communicates with the headset via the GSA 70 USB dongle using a reverse-engineered HID protocol.
.PP
The utility can display device information, monitor control events, show battery status, and enumerate available audio devices.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-device " " \fIauto|dongle|headset\fP
Select which device to communicate with. Defaults to \fBauto\fP which tries the dongle first, then the headset.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the program version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help message and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS info
Show device information including HID devices and audio devices.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output in JSON format.
.SS status
Show current headset status including notifications received.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output in JSON format.
.SS battery
Show battery status and LED indicator reference.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output in JSON format.
.SS controls
Control operations.
.TP
.B list
List all available controls.
.TP
.B get \fICONTROL\fP
Get the current value of a control (\fBvolume\fP, \fBmute\fP, or \fBsidetone\fP).
.TP
.B set \fICONTROL\fP \fIVALUE\fP
Set a control to a new value.
.SS monitor
Monitor control events in real-time. Press Ctrl+C to exit.
.TP
.B \-\-watch ", " \-w " " \fIall|battery|link\fP
Watch mode: \fIall\fP (default) shows every parsed frame and event,
\fIbattery\fP shows battery events with a 30 s poll fallback, \fIlink\fP
shows headset link/sub-device changes.
.TP
.B \-\-timeout ", " \-t " " \fISECONDS\fP
Exit automatically after SECONDS (0 = run forever, default).
.SS events
Show raw HID events from the device. Press Ctrl+C to exit.
.TP
.B \-\-count \fIN\fP
Capture exactly \fIN\fP events then exit automatically.
.SS protocol inspect
Show all known protocol opcodes and their status.
.SS log
Set logging level for debugging.
.TP
.B \-\-level ", " \-l " " \fIDEBUG|INFO|WARNING|ERROR|CRITICAL\fP
Set the logging level. Defaults to INFO.
.TP
.B \-\-message ", " \-m
Show a test message at each level.
.SS test audio
Run full-duplex audio quality tests.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (device not found, communication error, or invalid arguments).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Show device information:
.B gsp670 info
.TP
Show battery status:
.B gsp670 battery
.TP
List controls:
.B gsp670 controls list
.TP
Get volume level:
.B gsp670 controls get volume
.TP
Monitor control events:
.B gsp670 monitor
.TP
Capture 10 events and exit:
.B gsp670 events --count 10
.TP
Enable debug logging:
.B gsp670 log --level DEBUG
.TP
Show version:
.B gsp670 --version
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/gsp670/
User configuration directory (if implemented).
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/60-gsp670.rules
System udev rules for device access.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
Linux with Python 3.8 or higher
.TP
hidapi Python library
.TP
EPOS|Sennheiser GSP 670 headset with GSA 70 USB dongle
.SH BUGS
Report bugs to: https://github.com/mrcanofcatfood/gsp670-linux/issues
.PP
Battery status may not be available on all firmware versions.
.PP
Some systems may require udev rules to access the device.
